ations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU KATSUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC IND CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU, KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU KATSUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU, KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A reference signal is modulated by a modulating circuit (101), and the modulated signal is multiplied by a transmission weight. The resultant signal is subjected to radio transmission processing by transmission RF circuits (109 to 111). The reference signals are combined by a synthesizing circuit (119), and the synthesized signal is compared with the original reference signal by a correction control circuit (121). Thus, the corrections for phase and amplitude are determined. The phase and amplitude of the transmission signal are adjusted by using the corrections.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon l'invention, un signal de référence est modulé par un circuit de modulation (101), et le signal modulé est multiplié par un coefficient synaptique de transmission. Le signal résultant est soumis à un traitement de radiotransmission par des circuits RF de transmission (109 à 111). Les signaux de référence sont combinés par un circuit de synthétisation (119) et le signal synthétisé est comparé avec le signal de référence original par un circuit de contrôle de correction (121). On détermine ainsi les corrections de phase et d'amplitude. Ces corrections sont utilisées pour régler la phase et l'amplitude du signal de transmission.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>